<title>PERU: Peru net intl reserves rise to $8.499 bln Dec 4.</title>
<headline>Peru net intl reserves rise to $8.499 bln Dec 4.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Monday its net international reserves rose to $8.499 billion on December 4 from $8.412 billion a week earlier.</p>
<p>The bank's foreign exchange position, or total liquidity minus short- and long-term debt obligations, was $1.648 billion on December 4.</p>
<p>President Alberto Fujimori said last month the government expected Peru's international reserves to rise above $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $6.641 billion.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima Newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
